<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭăpāsōn</span></b> 
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ πασῶν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδῶν</span>), in music, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the whole octave</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5, 4,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut. 2, 22, 20</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 944</span></i>;
			so too, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭăpente</span></b>  = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ
				πέντε</span>, <i>a fifth</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 934
			al.</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭătessărōn</span></b>  =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διατεσσάρων</span>, <i>a
				fourth</i>, <i><span class="en">id. 2, §
			107</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5, 4, 8</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disdĭăpāsōn</span></b>  =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δὶς διὰ πασῶν</span>, <i>a double octave</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 22,
				20, § 84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2,
				§ 199 al.</span></i> (All these words should perhaps be
			written here, as in <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2,
			1</span></i>, in Greek letters.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
